speechtext:
I gave that information on the Main Estimates. Referring to Hansard of May 23, I find that the figures I gave were as follows: Of the employees in the department, 37.8 per cent are females in clerical positions which are not sought by returned soldiers. Of the remainder, 34.8 per cent have seen service in France; 4.7 per cent have seen service in England;
4.2	per cent have seen service in Canada;
2.2	per cent had been rejected or exempted; 6.6 per cent were over age or under age, and only 6.4 per cent were male employees who had not seen service in the Canadian Expeditionary Force.
